  "narration": {
    "transcript": "People aren't broken. They're rehearsed. A reaction, repeated often enough, becomes a pattern. And a pattern repeated long enough can begin to feel like identity. But familiar does not mean fixed. Identity is not destiny. Interrupt the old rehearsal. Pause before the familiar response. Practise something different. Repetition built the pattern. And repetition can build the way out."
  },
